Do not hardcode cloud credentials in client binaries. Obtain short-lived STS session tokens dynamically from a trusted backend.

Compliant AWS STS snippet:
AWSCredentialsProvider provider = new STSAssumeRoleSessionCredentialsProvider.Builder(roleArn, sessionName).build();

Remove plaintext credentials from source code. Use Android KeyStore and EncryptedSharedPreferences.

Compliant EncryptedSharedPreferences snippet:
MasterKey masterKey = new MasterKey.Builder(context)
    .setKeyScheme(MasterKey.KeyScheme.AES256_GCM)
    .build();
SharedPreferences securePrefs = EncryptedSharedPreferences.create(
    context, "secure_prefs", masterKey,
    EncryptedSharedPreferences.PrefKeyEncryptionScheme.AES256_SIV,
    EncryptedSharedPreferences.PrefValueEncryptionScheme.AES256_GCM
);

Never embed static JWT tokens into APK binaries. Fetch short-lived tokens from an authentication endpoint at runtime and store them in EncryptedSharedPreferences.

Compliant token storage:
securePrefs.edit().putString("auth_token", tokenFromAuthServer).apply();

Upgrade from DES/3DES to authenticated AES-256 in GCM mode.

